# lib/

Core implementation modules for cdsync, divided into shared primitives, configuration readers, and command handlers. Each module is sourced on-demand; common.sh loads first and establishes the colour scheme, logging, and classification vocabulary used throughout.

## Files

- `common.sh` -- shared primitives, colour definitions, and logging helpers
- `config.sh` -- reads cdsync.json and resolves venture configuration
- `target.sh` -- resolves $CDSYNC_TARGET directory path with precedence rules
- `drop.sh` -- defines drop contract: owned paths, structure validation, and preservation rules
- `frontmatter.sh` -- YAML front-matter parser for specs, index, and metadata files
- `specs.sh` -- reads and walks the spec library manifest
- `archive.sh` -- pre-flight validation and staging for zip and directory sources
- `scan.sh` -- computes blank counts and colour literals in a drop
- `cmd_bootstrap.sh` -- generates BOOTSTRAP-CD.md from tree state
- `cmd_brief.sh` -- assembles the brief for Claude Design from config and specs
- `cmd_check.sh` -- validates a drop against six rules (status, version, blanks, colours, coverage, classification)
- `cmd_import.sh` -- merges converted drop into target, preserving addenda
- `cmd_init.sh` -- initialises design system skeleton in existing repo
- `cmd_install.sh` -- replaces target with as-is drop, preserving gitignored content
- `cmd_new.sh` -- scaffolds a new venture with config and templates
- `cmd_site.sh` -- generates microsite from drop into target/site/
- `cmd_release.sh` -- manages version bumping and release ceremony
- `doctor.sh` -- validates installation and checks dependencies
